From 94c8fc19f28320d3f022da70d9b34b669fbdafbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:16:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use latest stable OpenSSL and compatible Rust bindings

Upgrade the Bazel integration to 4.0.1.bcr.0 and Rust openssl/openssl-sys
to 0.10.81/0.9.117. Keep the source-header regression and add a Rust
runtime regression covering the bundled library, hashing, and TLS setup.
Drop the crypto/init.c backport already present in OpenSSL 4.0.1.

Base: rust-v0.162.1, 092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d.
Prerequisites: preceding issue-61 native warning patches.

Red: the Rust regression against OpenSSL 4.0.1 with openssl-sys 0.9.111
fails in its build script because it rejects OpenSSL version 40000010.
Green: the same regression with openssl 0.10.81 and openssl-sys 0.9.117
passes. Compiler outputs are isolated between baseline and candidate.
The uncached native configuration-header and TLS/provider runtime tests
also pass, and the CLI version/help probe builds and executes.

Focused verification:
bazel test //tools/build-warnings/openssl:configuration_header_test
  //tools/build-warnings/openssl:ssl_init_test
  //tools/build-warnings/openssl:rust_bindings_test
  //tools/build-warnings/openssl:cli_probe
